In a message dated 11/13/2007 4:34:07 AM Central Standard Time, 
ecartis@digitalkingdom.org writes:


> Perhaps the error is in the word "equal" as well.  To say that all 
> cultures deserve respect does not necessarily require that all cultures 
> get equal respect.  Rather, it means that the range of respect that is 
> granted should always be above some minimal value, arising from the sum 
> of the minimum value of the respect due each individual person in that 
> culture merely for being a human being.
> 

The mere fact of being a human being is not sufficient grounds for any 
respect.  The worst people deserve no respect at all.  Strangers are accorded 
respect by giving them the benefit of the doubt.  Once they become known quantities, 
their actions and words signal how much respect they deserve.  

stevo   </HTML>
           
